**Job Description**
 Morgan Stanley Services Group, Inc. is seeking an Associate, Software Engineer in Alpharetta, GA to collaborate with business and product partners to understand business problems. The role involves analyzing business data to formulate appropriate data models, participating in data system architecture and design discussions, and developing software solutions in a lean\-agile methodology. Responsibilities also include creating technical documentation, developing code to manage high volumes of data, and deriving solutions for data integration engineers using various ETL tools. Telecommuting is permitted up to 2 days a week.




**Requirements**
* Requires a Master’s in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or a related field.
* Requires three (3\) years of experience in the position offered or three (3\) years as a Software Developer, Software Application Developer, or a related occupation.
* Requires three (3\) years of experience with the following skills:
* Formulating data models;
* Java;
* ETL tools including:
* Informatica;
* Datastage;
* Python;
* Spark.
* RDBMS systems including:
* Oracle;
* MS\-SQL;
* Teradata.
* Handling Big Data in systems including:
* Hadoop;
* HDFS;
* Hive.
* Agile methodologies;
* Shell scripts;
* Python scripts;
* PySpark scripts;
* ETL tools including:
* Python;
* Database SQL.


 Additional Information




 At Morgan Stanley, we manage and allocate capital for our clients in a way that is differentiated and has been successful for 90 years. Our core values include putting clients first, doing the right thing, leading with exceptional ideas, committing to diversity and inclusion, and giving back.




 Employees can expect to work alongside the best and brightest in an environment that fosters support and empowerment. Morgan Stanley provides comprehensive employee benefits and perks, along with opportunities for mobility within the business for those who demonstrate passion and determination.




 The expected base pay rates for the role will be between $161,000 and $161,000 per year. However, the base pay if hired will be determined on an individualized basis and is only part of the total compensation package, which may also include commission earnings, incentive compensation, discretionary bonuses, and other benefit programs.




 Morgan Stanley is an equal opportunity employer committed to maintaining a diverse workforce and an inclusive culture. For more information, please visit: https://www.morganstanley.com/people\-opportunities/eeo.




